nums.length = 2;                 // truncates
console.log(nums);
nums[5] = 6;                     // creates holes
console.log(nums, nums.length);
console.log(nums.at(-1), nums[nums.length - 1]);
[ 1, 2 ]
[ 1, 2, <3 empty items>, 6 ] 6
6 6
Checking and converting
console.log(Array.isArray([]), typeof []);
console.log([1, [2, 3]].toString(), String([null, undefined, 1]));
console.log([3, 1, 2].join(" < "), "a-b-c".split("-"));
true object
1,2,3 ,,1
3 < 1 < 2 [ ''a'', ''b'', ''c'' ]
How do you empty an array?
arr.length = 0 (mutates — every reference sees an empty array), arr.splice(0) (mutates, returns the removed items), or arr = [] (rebinds only this variable; other references keep the old contents).'), 'C'),
